.TH GOWORK 1 "2026-10-02" "gowork" "gowork Manual"
.SH NAME
gowork, gw \- git and GitHub workflow, per-directory identity, dev-shell setup
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gw
.I command
.RI [ args ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gowork
(short:
.BR gw )
puts three tools behind one command: the git and pull-request workflow that
used to be
.BR gp ,
the account and identity management that used to be
.B gp account
and
.BR "rigor identity" ,
and the shell features that used to be
.BR rigor .
The old names keep working.
.PP
A command
.B gw
doesn't know is handed to git, so
.B gw pull
is
.BR "git pull" .
gowork's own commands avoid git's names for that reason.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR pr ", " pl ", " pm
Pull requests: list, check out, merge, close, unmerge.
.B pl
and
.B pm
are short for
.B pr list
and
.BR "pr merge" .
See
.BR gp-pr (1).
.TP
.BR new ", " switch ", " sync ", " done ", " sweep ", " wsweep ", " haspr ", " release
Branch and worktree workflow; see each
.BR gp- <command>(1)
page.
.TP
.B fork sync\fR|\fBstatus\fR|\fBpr
Work with a fork of another repository (the
.I upstream
remote): catch its base branch up, here and on origin; compare it and your
branches with upstream; open a pull request to upstream. See
.BR gp-fork (1).
.TP
.B account setup\fR|\fBstatus\fR|\fBoff
Install, inspect or remove the
.B gh
and
.B aws
shims, git's credential routing and the Claude Code sandbox exclusions.
.TP
.B account add\fR|\fBbind\fR|\fBunbind\fR|\fBlist\fR|\fBkey\fR|\fBregister\fR|\fBcheck\fR|\fBsweep
Per-directory GitHub accounts and their SSH keys; see
.BR gp-account (1).
.TP
.B aws bind \fIprofile\fR [\fIdir\fR] | \fBaws unbind \fR[\fIdir\fR]
The AWS profile a directory uses.
.TP
.B shell enable\fR|\fBdisable\fR|\fBstatus\fR|\fBdoctor\fR|\fBinit
Shell features: autovenv, pyf, envup; see
.BR rigor (1).
.TP
.B notify setup\fR|\fBstatus\fR|\fBtest\fR|\fBoff
Phone notifications when a Claude Code or Codex turn ends.
.TP
.B sleep on\fR|\fBoff\fR|\fBstatus
Toggle
.B pmset disablesleep
(needs sudo).
.TP
.B browser setup\fR|\fBsync\fR|\fBstatus\fR|\fBoff\fR|\fBopen \fIaccount url
Open GitHub links in the Chrome profile signed in to the right account, via
Finicky as the default browser, with rules generated from the accounts and
their bindings.
.TP
.BR feed " [" \fIwhen\fR "] [" \-e "] [" \-g "] [" \-\fIN\fR "] [" \-\-once ]
Your latest merged and closed PRs, oldest first, each tagged
.B [MERGED]
or
.BR [CLOSED] ;
the listing is
.B gp pr latest
(see
.BR gp-pr (1)).
In a terminal it then stays open and adds each PR as it merges or closes,
until Ctrl-C;
.BR \-\-once ,
.BR \-c ,
a window with an end, or output into a pipe prints it once instead.
.B \-e
shows everyone's in the repository,
.B \-g
yours in every repository and account.
.TP
.B feed review
Go through the updates waiting to be posted to Slack. Each starts kept; space
withholds it (or keeps it again),
.B e
rewords it in
.BR $EDITOR ,
.B p
posts one digest per channel after asking, and
.B q
leaves them all queued. A withheld update is remembered and never comes back.
.TP
.BR "feed collect" " [" \-\-quiet ]
Queue the PRs you've merged, in any repository and under any
.B gh
account, since the last collect (a day back the first time), and send a phone
notification through
.B gw notify
when there's something new. Only repositories with a route are queued.
.TP
.BR "feed channel add" " \fIname\fR [\fIwebhook-url\fR] | " "feed channel rm" " \fIname"
A Slack channel to post to, by its incoming webhook. Without the URL it's
read from standard input, which keeps it out of shell history.
.TP
.BR "feed route" " \fIowner/repo\fR|\fIowner/*\fR \fIchannel\fR | " "feed route rm" " \fIpattern"
Post that repository's updates, or a whole owner's, to that channel. An exact
repository beats its owner's route.
.TP
.BR "feed setup" " [" \-\-at " \fIHH:MM\fR] | " "feed status" " | " "feed off"
Run
.B feed collect
every day at that time (17:00) with launchd; show channels, routes, schedule
and what's waiting; stop the daily run.
.B git config \-\-global gowork.feedHeading
sets the digest's first line, which is otherwise your name.
.TP
.BR migrate " [" \-\-dry\-run ]
Point an existing rigor/gitplus setup at gowork: rc-file source lines and
completion path, Claude Code hooks, Codex's notify program, identity shims,
and command links from a checkout install. Drops the retired
.I ghswitch
hook. Edited files are backed up as
.IR <file>.gowork-bak .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/rigor/
Configuration, kept under its original name.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/rigor/identity/bin/
The gh and aws shims.
.TP
.I ~/.config/rigor/feed/
.B gw feed
channels (webhook URLs, mode 600) and routes.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/rigor/feed/
.B gw feed
queue, decisions, and the daily collect's log.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gp-pr (1),
.BR gp-account (1),
.BR rigor (1),
.BR git (1),
.BR gh (1)
